Conclusion
You have successfully implemented APC-based process injection on Linux using open-source tools. This lab demonstrated:

Process Memory Manipulation: Used ptrace to attach to and modify target processes
Dynamic Code Injection: Allocated executable memory and injected custom payloads
APC Simulation: Implemented APC-like behavior through register manipulation
Payload Execution: Successfully executed injected code within target process context
This technique is fundamental to understanding advanced process manipulation, memory forensics, and security research. The skills learned here apply to malware analysis, penetration testing, and defensive security measures.

